This is a very unfortunate aspect of the current topology aware hints heuristic. In a cluster with 3 equivalent zones, [hints will not be allocated when a Service has 4, 5, 8, or 11 endpoints](https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1_4QyfQEcnEWYpcmUc1Q6cjgkLMhMqpTgok2UUpOmUhE/edit?resourcekey=0-k7XjENYqtAyBfm12lDq0KQ#gid=0). Of course zones are not always equivalent, and there are not always 3 zones in a cluster, so there will be many exceptions to this.

@gauravkghildiyal is working on a new heuristic for Topology Aware Hints that would keep all traffic in zone if _any_ healthy endpoints were present (https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/121060). That approach has its own limitations, but is likely preferable in many cases, it all depends on risk tolerance. 

Unfortunately I think this is actually the heuristic working as intended, so I don't think there's a lot we can change here. The overarching idea with the existing heuristic was to have something that kept traffic in the same zone whenever it was reasonably safe, and the overload threshold was a rather rudimentary way to achieve that.

